From 87c47b4bd82c17a963a1774a6ad32c57f58560b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:24:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Speed up light traversal, class tables and Q10 lookups
 without changing results

Unroll the Amanatides-Woo axes in path_sum_b, locate a ray's start once,
reuse each leaf's footprint from the daily grid fit, compute the class
table's temperature terms once per table, and cache every Q10 factor of
the hour. All bit-identical: golden hashes unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYHSSvnop11Bd1JLmA2mJz
